  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scoping study Sand Motor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The scoping study project&apos;s focus is:1.	To assess the possibility of using the Sand Motor concept to combat the erosion risks along the Mediterranean coasts in Egypt,2.	How to integrate the Sand Motor concept with other protection systems and the ongoing Integrated Coastal Zone Management (ICZM) plan along this coast to provide a resilient and sustainable protection, and3.	To define follow-up on this scoping mission.In case of a positive assessment the contours of a Terms of Reference (ToR) for a follow-up study or feasibility study should be drafted, having in mind that financing of the implementation might be requested through Green Climate Funding (GCF).In case of a negative assessment, recommendations have to be drafted to improve the ongoing coastal protection efforts, like the &#x2018;Enhancing climate change adaptation in the north coast and Nile delta regions in Egypt&#x2019; project (ECCADP).</narrative>
  </description>
